{title: Running From the Lord}
{subtitle: Jonah 1:1–16; 2:1}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 143}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×25

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The word of the Lord came to Jonah one day
Go to Nineveh, preach against her ways
But Jonah ran down to Joppa instead
Paid for a ship bound for Tarshish ahead
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Running from the Lord, [Cm]running from the Lord
[Eb]You can't outrun him on [F]the sea or the [Gm]shore
Running from the [Cm]Lord, running from the [Eb]Lord
Jonah went [F]down, down, [Gm]down
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The Lord sent a wind and a terrible storm
The sailors cried out, every man to his god
Jonah lay sleeping deep down in the hold
Throw me in the sea and it will be calm
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [D] | [D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They [Gm]threw him overboard and the sea grew still
[Eb]The Lord sent a fish to do his will
[Cm]Three days and three nights in the belly of the whale
[D]Jonah learned to pray where his running failed
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Cm] | [Eb] | [F] | ×2
| [Gm] | ×10
